    description: "Three producers emit an external_symbol edge target whose id fails the validator's id_format check and that no filed item covers. Found by the 45-tree fleet measurement run for INV-dulah (dev a35aeb56aa, hypergumbo survey --include-docs; record: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026/pr2/fleet_idformat.txt). Each was re-run on dev 425477b693 on 2026-11-16.\n\n1. JavaScript, empty path slot. express (curriculum_repos/express): 3 nodes, 364 call edges.\n   ids: javascript::0-0:default:external_symbol, javascript::0-0:static:external_symbol, javascript::0-0:urlencoded:external_symbol\n   Source: examples/content-negotiation/index.js line 3 is `var express = require('../../');` and line 4 calls `express()`; examples/cookies/index.js line 22 calls `express.urlencoded()`; examples/ejs/index.js line 31 calls `express.static(...)`. The required module is the repository root directory, and the edge dst carries an empty path slot. Validator message: double_colon_separator (INV-sadiv).\n   Repro: hypergumbo survey <express> --out m.json --include-docs; count nodes whose id contains '::0-0:'.\n\n2. Tcl, empty path slot and empty name slot. git-gui (whole_bunch_of_repos/git/git-gui): 1 node, 1 call edge.\n   id: tcl::0-0::external_symbol\n   Source: the edge is from make_toplevel (lib/class.tcl 144-175) at line 159, which reads `regsub -all {::} $this {__} w`. Which word the analyzer takes for the callee was not traced.\n\n3. Markdown, a newline in the path slot. poetry (curriculum_repos/poetry): 1 node, 1 references edge.\n   id (repr): 'markdown:\\nhttps_//packaging.python.org/en/latest/guides/making-a-pypi-friendly-readme/:0-0:making-a-pypi-friendly-readme:external_symbol'\n   Source: docs/pyproject.md line 518 opens a link `[recommendations for a PyPI-friendly README](` and the URL is on line 519. The link target is used with its leading newline. Validator message: \"does not match the canonical schema: unknown\".\n\nAlso seen, not flagged by the validator: Markdown link nodes whose NAME slot holds a newline when the link text wraps across lines (git-gui README.md line 3: 'markdown:README.md:3-3:Git source control management\\ntools:link' and one more; poetry docs/pyproject.md line 529: '...:Description\\nfield:link'). An id with a newline in it breaks any line-oriented reader of ids.\n\nWhat is asked: a general fix at each producer (an edge dst is built by the id helpers with a non-empty path slot and a name with no newline, or no edge is emitted), not a patch for these four trees. Not measured: how many other analyzers can emit an empty path or name slot; the fleet found these on 3 of 45 trees.\n\nOther id_format classes from the same fleet run have their own items: a colon in the name slot (JS/TS event-string names, 36 nodes) is WI-dodom-rudol-sihan-vohif-novin-mogum-naraf-hagug; the <unknown> path slot (26 nodes, LaTeX / Robot / Meson / Fortran) is WI-tatop-nalor-zokif-jipug-furip-jisun-pogar-fulog and, for LaTeX, INV-zipaj-zutuk-fajak-donod-daziz-tudiv-fipop-zudit."  # 642a
